      "side": 1,
      "message": "This looks generally good. I do have one concern. We are adding use of RPC messages between Ganesha nodes for transparent state migration. I haven\u0027t seen the code yet so I\u0027m not sure where it\u0027s setting up its socket, but if done through RPC dispatcher, we would want it binding to a different interface. Of course we could exclude that, but something to think about.\n\nAlso what about trunking that uses several interfaces? Or is there a virtual interface that handles the trunking?       \n\nOf course none of these concerns are any more than would apply to BindAddr...",
