      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for the review!\n\nTo answer your question about trunking: yes, the OS handles this by exposing a virtual interface (like bond0 or team0). The user would simply specify that virtual interface name in `Interface_Name`, and it will handle the underlying physical interfaces transparently. See https://docs.redhat.com/en/documentation/red_hat_enterprise_linux/8/html/configuring_and_managing_networking/configuring-network-bonding_configuring-and-managing-networking for how it can be configured. I will note that I have not played around with this, and I don\u0027t know how it will affect.\n\nRegarding the upcoming state migration: Since this patch exactly mirrors the existing scope and limitations of `Bind_Addr`, any future migration features that need to bypass the global `NFS_CORE_PARAMS` parameters can just introduce their own dedicated config overrides when that code actually lands.",
